{title: 305 - Give Me Jesus}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #305 • GIVE ME JESUS • 14.11.8.10}
{lyricist: American Negro Spiritual}
{composer: Alma Blackmon}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 305}
{meta: tune GIVE ME JESUS}
{meta: meter 14.11.8.10}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]In the [Dm]morning, [C/G]when I rise, In the [Em]morning, when [Dm/F]I [F]rise
[G7/F]In the morning, [F]when [Dm]I [Em]rise, [C/G]Give [Em]me Jesus.
[F]Give me [G7/F]Jesus, [C/E]Give me Jesus.
[C/G]You can have all [G]this world, [Am/E]Give me [G7/F]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Give me [G7/F]Jesus.
[Dm/A]Give me [C7/A#]Jesus,
[C7/A#]Give [A#]me [Am]Jesus.
[Am]You can [C/G]have [F]all [G7/F]this [C/E]world,
[C/E]Just give me Jesus.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Dark [Dm]mid-night [C/E]was [Em]my [Dm/F]cry,
[G7/F]Dark mid-night [Em]was [C/G]my [Em]cry,
[F]Dark midnight [C/E]was my cry,
[C/G]Give me [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Just [Dm]about [C/E]the break [Em]of [Dm/F]day,
[G7/F]Just about [Dm]the [Em]break of day,
[F]Just about [G7/F]the [C/E]break of day,
[C/G]Give me [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Oh, [Dm]when [C/G]I come [Em]to [Dm/F]die,
[G7/F]Oh, when [F]I [Em]come [C/G]to [Em]die,
[F]Oh, when [G7/F]I [C/E]come to die,
[C/G]Give me [G]Jesus.
{end_of_verse}
